# Engagement runtime data (per-target recon, results, chain state)
# Only .md documents are tracked under engagements/ — anything generated at
# runtime can carry target data (origin IP, WAF product, findings) and must
# never be committed. Adding the rule BEFORE any writer exists means a first
# test write can never reach the index.
engagements/*/
# Tracked under engagements/ are documents only. '!engagements/*.md' un-ignores
# any *entry* ending in .md, including a directory - an engagement for a target
# like app.md (Moldova) would then expose its whole tree. So: deny every file
# that could hold engagement data, at any depth, before re-including documents.
engagements/**/*.json
engagements/**/*.csv
engagements/**/*.har
engagements/**/*.html
engagements/**/*.txt
engagements/**/*.log
engagements/**/*.lock
engagements/**/*.tmp
# Re-include tracked documents last, so the rules above cannot re-ignore them.
!engagements/*.md
!engagements/*/*.md
!engagements/*/*/*.md
engagements/**/*.json
engagements/**/*.csv
engagements/**/*.har
engagements/**/*.html
engagements/**/evidence/
engagements/**/.lock
